 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** The MLP $g_\theta$ is invoked once per visible level, not once per visible anchor. The cost of MLP evaluation scales with the number of visible levels $|L_V|$ [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** HAC adds 4,160 parameters via the shared two-layer MLP (hidden dimension $d=32$) [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Performance:** On the Mill19-Building scene, HAC yields a PSNR improvement of +1.91 dB over the baseline [S1, unofficial]. Training time increases slightly due to per-view aggregation, but the net rendering speed improves because HAC reduces the number of decoded and rasterized Neural Gaussians by roughly 35% [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Time Complexity:** The MLP $g_\theta$ is invoked once per visible level, not once per visible anchor [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Memory Complexity:** HAC adds 4,160 parameters via the shared two-layer MLP with hidden dimension $d=32$ [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Performance:** On the Mill19-Building scene, HAC yields a PSNR improvement of +1.91 dB over the baseline [S1, unofficial].
 *   **Granularity Trade-offs:**
     *   **Per-Level (Default):** Faster (~20% faster in training) and better for dense repetitive structures (e.g., +1.06 dB on Building) [S1, unofficial].
-    *   **Per-Anchor:** Computes a distinct $\delta_i$ for every anchor via spatial lookup. Cost grows linearly with $|V|$ [S1, unofficial].
+    *   **Per-Anchor:** Computes a distinct $\delta_i$ for every anchor via spatial lookup [S1, unofficial].
 *   **Strengths:** Alleviates feature isolation; low parameter overhead; compatible with various backbones (CityGS-X, Octree-GS, Proxy-GS) [S1, unofficial].
 *   **Limitations:** Relies on the underlying octree structure; performance gain depends on scene topology [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## Background
-Hierarchical Anchor Coupling was introduced in the paper "TopoGS: Topology-Aware Anchor Feature Aggregation for Large-Scale 3D Gaussian Splatting" [S1, unofficial]. It was developed to address the lack of cross-level gradient pathways in existing anchor-based octree pipelines. The method is integrated into the TopoGS framework and has been shown to transfer effectively to other structured 3DGS backbones like Octree-GS and Proxy-GS [S1, unofficial].
